-- title:
--   The crossing involution sends U to V
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Consider the ring of formal power series in two variables $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ and its ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W π` generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, and let `UVCrossingModel W π` be the quotient ring, with `U π` and `V π` the residue classes of the variables $X_0$ and $X_1$ respectively. Let `uvSwapEquiv` be the ring automorphism of $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ obtained by renaming the indices along the transposition $0 \leftrightarrow 1$ of $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$; since it preserves the ideal $(X_0X_1 - C(\pi))$, it descends to the ring automorphism `crossingSwap π` of `UVCrossingModel W π`. The theorem asserts the single equality in `UVCrossingModel W π`
--   $$\mathrm{crossingSwap}\,\pi\,(U\,\pi) = V\,\pi,$$
--   that is, the descended variable-exchange automorphism of $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ carries the class of $u$ to the class of $v$. No hypothesis on $\pi$ (such as being a nonunit or a nonzerodivisor) is required.
--
--   This records one of the defining values of the branch-exchange involution of the crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$, which serves as the local model at a supersingular point of the special fibre of a $\Gamma_0(p)$-modular curve, the involution playing the role of the Atkin–Lehner involution exchanging the two branches $u=0$ and $v=0$. It is used in showing that `U π` does not lie in the fixed subring of `crossingSwap π` and in computing the image of the ideal generated by `U π` under this involution.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_crossingSwap_U.lean

